#~ msgid ""
#~ "There are no panels for one "
#~ "machine only: a ZX Evolution with "
#~ "TSConf or BaseConf uses the same "
#~ "panels as any other machine."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The **Tape** panel draws the tape "
#~ "signal around the place the tape "
#~ "is at. The red vertical line is"
#~ " now: on its left is the signal"
#~ " that has played, on its right "
#~ "what comes next. The picture covers "
#~ "about two milliseconds of tape at "
#~ "the machine's speed."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The **FDC** panel shows the floppy "
#~ "disk controller in its left and "
#~ "middle columns and the drive it "
#~ "works with in the right one. It"
#~ " is there only on a machine "
#~ "with a disk interface (see [Disks "
#~ "and drives](disks.md)). All numbers are "
#~ "hex; a flag is 1 or 0."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "A plain ZX uses the first 16 "
#~ "squares. With ULA+ in use, the "
#~ "first 64 are the colors the "
#~ "program set. The ZX Evolution with "
#~ "TSConf fills all 256 from its own"
#~ " palette memory. The ATM Turbo 2+,"
#~ " the ZX Evolution with BaseConf and"
#~ " the Profi v5 set their colors "
#~ "through ports, and the colors a "
#~ "program sets show here as it sets"
#~ " them."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Show in its own window** - moves"
#~ " the panel into the **Screen** "
#~ "window."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Show in its own window** - moves"
#~ " the panel into the **Sound Chips**"
#~ " window."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The target button - jumps to the"
#~ " drive, the track and the byte "
#~ "the head is at now."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Show in its own window** - moves"
#~ " the panel into the **ZX Evolution**"
#~ " window; pressed in here, as the "
#~ "panel is in it."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The button at the top right of "
#~ "the panel, **Show in its own "
#~ "window**, moves the panel into a "
#~ "window of its own, **ZX Evolution**. "
#~ "In the window the button is "
#~ "pressed in; click it again, or "
#~ "close the window, to put the panel"
#~ " back in the Debugger. While the "
#~ "panel is out, its tab in the "
#~ "Debugger says so, with a **Bring "
#~ "it back** button. Unlike the **Screen**"
#~ " and **Sound Chips** windows, this "
#~ "one has no command in the "
#~ "**Debug** menu."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The button at the top right of "
#~ "each panel, **Show in its own "
#~ "window**, does the same. In the "
#~ "window it is pressed in; click it"
#~ " again, or close the window, to "
#~ "put the panel back in the "
#~ "Debugger. While the panel is out, "
#~ "its tab in the Debugger says so,"
#~ " with a **Bring it back** or "
#~ "**Bring them back** button."
#~ msgstr ""

